   "text": {
    "L1": "Grandfather gives Mario an invisible chair as a test. The chair cannot really hold him up.",
    "L2": "Mario falls again and again, while some classmates laugh. He keeps trying, so he is determined.",
    "L3": "Guneet, Asma and Deepa hold Mario up when he falls. They are the friends who truly care.",
    "L4": "The magic was not in the chair. The three friends were really holding Mario up.",
    "L5": "Grandfather was clever because his test showed who cared and who enjoyed Mario's bad luck.",
    "L6": "The story's message is simple: true friends help us when we fall. People who laugh at our bad luck are not true friends.",
    "L7": "Use who for people: Mario had three true friends who held him up. Also remember: helpful and careful have one l in -ful.",
    "L8": "Now put the main events in the story's order. Tap each event from first to last."
   },
